<div class="bt">Likutay Halachos — Orach Chaim, Volume 2</div>
<div class="ht">Hilchos Tefilas HaMinchah [Laws of the Afternoon Prayer]<br>Halachah 3<br><span style="font-size:.95rem;font-weight:400">Based on <span class="lr">LM I:66</span> (<i>Vihi Na Pi Shnayim</i>)</span></div>

<div class="sn">Introduction — The Spirit of <i>Mashiach</i> and the Opening of the Hands</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Halachah</span>: The time of <span class="h">Minchah</span> is after six hours.</div>

<div class="p">Based on what Rabbainu <span class="h">zichrono livrachah</span> writes in the teaching "<span class="h">Vihi Na Pi Shnayim B'Ruchacha Ailay</span>" (<span class="lr">LM I:66</span>): there is an aspect of <span class="h">charon af</span> [fierce anger], and one must sweeten and clarify the smoke of the <span class="h">charon af</span> so that it becomes the aspect of <span class="h">ruach aviri</span> [an airy spirit] — the spirit of <span class="h">Mashiach</span>. Before it arrives at the aspect of the hands, it is the aspect of "before existence" [<span class="h">kodem hahavayah</span>]. The essential existence is when this spirit arrives within the hands. Initially the two hands are one — the aspect of "before Creation." One must bring from potential to actual — opening and cutting the hands so there is a right hand and a left hand. This is the aspect of Creation — bringing from potential to actual. They are the two spirits — the <span class="h">pi shnayim</span> [double portion] mentioned above: <span class="h">ruach d'l'aila</span> [the spirit above] and <span class="h">ruach d'l'sata</span> [the spirit below]. The aspect of the two <span class="h">Yuds</span> — a <span class="h">Yud</span> at the beginning and a <span class="h">Yud</span> at the end — in the two Names [<span class="h">Y-AKDONK-Y</span>], with six letters in between, the aspect of <span class="h">pesach</span> [opening]: <span class="v">"You open Your hands [<i>yadecha</i>] — Your <i>Yuds</i>"</span> — through the <span class="h">Vav</span> (= the opening), the hands (= the <span class="h">Yuds</span>) are opened and divided. Then it is the aspect of Creation — bringing from potential to actual. See all this there well.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 1 — The Order of the Day: Night, Dawn, Morning, and <i>Minchah</i></div>

<div class="p">This is the aspect of the order of the day. At night, in darkness — <span class="mx">"when deep sleep falls upon men and the masters of judgment awaken"</span> — this is the aspect of <span class="h">charon af</span>. The <span class="h">charon af</span> (= the smoke) must be clarified: <span class="v">"smoke rose in His anger."</span> This is accomplished through the smoke of the <span class="h">korbanos</span>, which ascended at night to subdue and sweeten all the masters of judgment (as brought) — clarifying and repairing the smoke of the <span class="h">charon af</span> through the smoke of the <span class="h">korbanos</span>. The smoke went out toward the north (as brought) — where all the masters of judgment and anger reside: <span class="v">"from the north evil shall open forth"</span> — the aspect of anger: <span class="v">"remove anger from your heart and remove evil from your flesh."</span> Through this, an abundance of sustenance is drawn: <span class="v">"from the north gold shall come"</span> — when the anger of the north side is sweetened, wealth and sustenance are drawn from there (as Rabbainu writes in the above teaching; see there well).</div>

<div class="p">Then the smoke of the <span class="h">charon af</span> is repaired and clarified, becoming a holy <span class="h">ruach aviri</span> — the spirit of <span class="h">Mashiach</span>. This is the north wind that blows upon David's <span class="h">kinor</span> [harp] at midnight — the revelation of the kingdom of <span class="h">Mashiach</span> (= the kingdom of David), revealed at midnight. It is a northern wind — revealed specifically from the north, from the clarification of the smoke and anger in the north. At midnight is the beginning of the revelation of the spirit of <span class="h">Mashiach</span>. But it is still night and dark — the spirit has not yet reached the aspect of existence, the hands, until daylight. At dawn, the spirit is revealed in the aspect of the hands: <span class="v">"let there be light"</span> and <span class="v">"there was light"</span> — right hand and left hand.</div>

<div class="p">Initially: <span class="v">"the earth was void and chaos and darkness"</span> — the aspect of anger, judgment, <span class="h">charon af</span>. From there specifically the spirit of <span class="h">Mashiach</span> is clarified: <span class="v">"the spirit of G-d hovered"</span> — <span class="mx">"this is the spirit of <i>Mashiach</i>"</span> (Zohar, <span class="h">Vayechi</span> 240) — drawn from the clarification of the darkness and smoke. Then: <span class="v">"G-d said: let there be light, and there was light"</span> — the two hands (as brought). The spirit is drawn into the hands — then the essential existence: <span class="v">"let there be light."</span> <span class="v">"G-d saw the light, that it was good — and He stood and stored it for the future"</span> — this light will not be revealed until <span class="h">Mashiach</span> comes and the World to Come, for this light is the spirit of <span class="h">Mashiach</span>. <span class="v">"G-d separated between the light and the darkness; G-d called the light 'day'"</span> — afterward He brought from potential to actual: the two spirits are revealed (= the two <span class="h">Yuds</span>: beginning of thought and end of action = day and night, as known). At first they were intermingled (being one); afterward they were separated and opened. See the above teaching well. Then comes the essential Creation. <span class="v">"There was evening and there was morning"</span> — the essential beginning of Creation and the revelation of the hands through the aspect of <span class="v">"He separated."</span></div>

<div class="p">At daylight (= <span class="v">"let there be light"</span> and <span class="v">"there was light"</span>), the spirit of <span class="h">Mashiach</span> is revealed in the hands. Therefore we then don <span class="h">tefillin</span> — where the kingdom of <span class="h">Mashiach</span> is revealed in the knot of the <span class="h">tefillin</span> (as brought). The <span class="h">tefillin</span> of the head and of the hand (arm) are the aspects of right and left — the hands, the two <span class="h">Yuds</span>. The essential <span class="h">tefillin</span> are during <span class="h">Krias Shma</span> and <span class="h">tefilah</span>: <span class="h">Krias Shma</span> is the <span class="h">Daled</span> of <span class="h">Echad</span> (= the kingdom of <span class="h">Mashiach</span>), and <span class="h">tefilah</span> too is the kingdom of <span class="h">Mashiach</span> (as Rabbainu writes in <span class="lr">LM I:2</span>: the essential weapon of <span class="h">Mashiach</span> is <span class="h">tefilah</span>).</div>

<div class="p">In the morning (<span class="h">Shacharis</span>), as long as the aspect of night (= end of action, the <span class="h">Yud</span> at the end) has not yet begun to be revealed — it is still the aspect of "before bringing from potential to actual." One must bring from potential to actual — to reveal the aspect of night. This is <span class="h">Tefilas HaMinchah</span>, after midday, extending through the last six hours. After midday, as the evening shadows incline, one must reveal the aspect of night — bringing from potential to actual, in the aspect of the opening of the hands. This is <span class="h">Tefilas HaMinchah</span> — in the middle of the day, between <span class="h">Shacharis</span> and <span class="h">Arvis</span>, between day and night, between the two <span class="h">Yuds</span>. It is in the aspect of <span class="h">pesach</span> [opening] — the six letters between the two <span class="h">Yuds</span>. Therefore its time is the [last] six hours — through <span class="h">Tefilas HaMinchah</span> one brings from potential to actual, and day and night (= the two <span class="h">Yuds</span>) are revealed.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore, then harsh judgment prevails — the essential arousal of judgments is at the time of bringing from potential to actual, when they accuse (as at the time of Creation: <span class="mx">"what is man..."</span>). They also arouse to draw sustenance from the holiness, since the holiness has descended and extended downward (as known). This is what Rabbainu writes there: the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span>'s hold comes from the falling of the cutting and opening of the hands — <span class="v">"they were cut off from Your hand"</span> — their hold is from the <span class="h">pesach</span> (= bringing from potential to actual). Therefore they are aroused at <span class="h">Minchah</span> time.</div>

<div class="p">Therefore there is no <span class="h">Krias Shma</span> at <span class="h">Minchah</span> — only at <span class="h">Shacharis</span> and <span class="h">Arvis</span>. The essential spirit of <span class="h">Mashiach</span> (encompassing the <span class="h">pi shnayim</span>, the two <span class="h">Yuds</span>) is only in <span class="h">Shacharis</span> and <span class="h">Arvis</span> (day and night = the two <span class="h">Yuds</span>). These are the <span class="h">Krias Shma</span> of morning and evening — the <span class="h">Daled</span> of <span class="h">Echad</span> (= the <span class="h">Yud</span>: the ends of the <span class="h">Daled</span> = a <span class="h">Yud</span>, the two <span class="h">Yuds</span>). At <span class="h">Minchah</span>, one needs only to bring from potential to actual — in the aspect of <span class="h">pesach</span>: <span class="v">"You open Your hands."</span> This is done solely through <span class="h">tefilah</span> (= the aspect of opening): <span class="v">"Hashem, open my lips."</span> <span class="h">Tefilah</span> is the aspect of <span class="v">"You open Your hands and satisfy"</span> — we ask and pray that He open His hand and satisfy us by His will. Therefore at <span class="h">Minchah</span>, only <span class="h">tefilah</span> is needed.</div>

<div class="sn">§ 2 — Eliyahu at <i>Minchah</i>: Bringing from Potential to Actual</div>

<div class="p">This is: <span class="mx">"one should always be careful with <i>Tefilas HaMinchah</i>, for Eliyahu was answered only at <i>Minchah</i>."</span> Eliyahu needed then to subdue the overpowering of the <span class="h">Sitra Achra</span> and idol-worshippers. He prayed <span class="h">Minchah</span> specifically — their essential hold being from there (= <span class="v">"they were cut off from Your hand"</span>). Eliyahu overpowered and prayed <span class="h">Minchah</span> in its tikun — to subdue them at their root. Specifically at <span class="h">Minchah</span> time he subdued them.</div>

<div class="p">This was accomplished specifically through Eliyahu — for the <span class="h">pi shnayim</span> mentioned above is drawn from Eliyahu, as written: <span class="v">"let there be a double portion [<i>pi shnayim</i>] of your spirit upon me"</span> — said regarding Eliyahu. Through him the kingdom of <span class="h">Mashiach</span> is revealed. Therefore Eliyahu is appointed to herald the future redemption, revealing the kingdom of <span class="h">Mashiach</span>. Eliyahu specifically was careful with <span class="h">Tefilas HaMinchah</span> and was answered — for <span class="h">Minchah</span> is the aspect of bringing from potential to actual: the essential revelation of the hands and the <span class="h">Yuds</span> — the aspect of <span class="h">Mashiach</span>, may he come speedily in our days, <span class="h">amain</span>.</div>

<div class="p"><span class="h">Minchah</span> is the aspect of <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> — the creation of the world. Yitzchak established <span class="h">Tefilas HaMinchah</span>; therefore then judgment prevails (= Yitzchak). It is the aspect of <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> (= the <span class="h">Gevuros</span> of Yitzchak). On <span class="h">Rosh HaShanah</span> the world was created — therefore <span class="h">Minchah</span> is the aspect of Creation: bringing from potential to actual.</div>

<div class="cn">✦ End of Hilchos Tefilas HaMinchah, Halachah 3 ✦<br><i>Na Nach Nachma Nachman May'Uman</i></div>

  </div>
